From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:40:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/39] DSel model: price DFlash2 from its rounds as they ran
 (table key r)

With G6_S2_DSEL_MODEL the K-stop MTP is priced at its real rate (on
structured text ~0.057 tokens/ms: four tokens per v4 + m + 2e), while
DFlash2 kept SpecLen's position-rate estimate, whose seed prior
compounds over seven positions (a full block: 6.1 tokens at prior 4,
7.3 at 1) and which learns only from probes while on MTP. Once a dip
moved a structured request to MTP, coming back needed 0.066 tokens/ms
(the 15 % margin), about 6.9 tokens per block: out of reach, so it
stayed on MTP (fleet: structured -21 %). Fixed-K pricing counted MTP
as two drafts (<= 0.043) and came back.

Table key r: DFlash2's tokens per ms = the request's DFlash2 rounds'
committed tokens over their table cost (verify k + 1 rows + d), a
scored probe counting as a round verifying K drafts; the evidence ages
by r per MTP round so the probes after a dip decide (0.95: about two at
probe 32). Before any DFlash2 round the position rates still decide.
Rank-invariant: tokens, accept counts and the table only. Host test:
structured with a dip fixed-K 0.0632, model 0.0596, model + r 0.0652
tokens/ms; prose unchanged. Off: the steps of before.
